# Laravel API

- Validation lives in Form Requests. Controllers stay thin and declare return types.
- Output goes through API Resources, not hand-built arrays.
- Business rules live in services or policies. Interfaces go in `app/Contracts` and are bound in
  `AppServiceProvider::$bindings`.
- New persistence goes through a repository. Use backed enums and readonly value objects instead
  of loose arrays.
- No queries in loops: eager load or aggregate (`withCount`, subqueries). List endpoints are bounded.
- Wrap writes that touch more than one table in a transaction.
- New migrations are named with today's date. Never edit a migration that has already run.

## Good

```php
public function classify(ClassifyRequest $request): ClassificationResource
{
    return new ClassificationResource($this->classifier->classify($request->message()));
}

CustomerRequest::query()->withCount('notes')->with('latestNote')->latest()->limit(100)->get();
```

## Bad

```php
public function classify(Request $request)
{
    $message = $request->input('message');        // validation inline
    if (str_contains($message, 'refund')) { ... } // business rule in controller
    return ['category' => 'billing'];          // loose array, no resource
}

foreach (CustomerRequest::all() as $r) { $r->notes()->get(); } // N+1, unbounded
```
